Z||000003||BAM-BAM||07-15-2001||02:10 AM||||  Well, I made it back alive. First things first. For those of you who have never had the pleasure of meeting Jorge, and as those who have can attest, He is a super person. It's hard enough to trust people over the internet, esspecialy when you are dealing with autos (I know, I have been burned a couple of times). I know that there was a bit of aprehension on both sides of this deal. Afterall, we had never met or really corresponded much if any for that matter. Yet he took the chance and trusted a stranger and I did likewise. It turned out to be a risk well worth taking. Jorge is an awesome person, thanks Jorge. <BR>  Ok for the details. I left at 6:00 this morning and arriveed in Dana Point at exactly 10:00 AM. I had a little seaside lunch with my son and met Jorge at 11:45. The transaction was smooth and quick. Actually, it was to quick. I could have stayed longer just to hash out the Forum with Jorge. Anyway, after dicounting the price $100.00 because the car needs new front rotors, I was on my way. After getting fuel we headed out at 1:00PM. The drive was very smooth and the car handled perfectly. I even stretched it out a couple of times to test what Jorge had told me. At 80MPH it kicks hard when you put the peddle down. It has awesome high speed accelleration. I averaged 27+MPG on fuel from Dana Point to Baker California (194 Miles) on 7.1 Gals. Now that is amazing to me since I only get 147 miles to a tank of gas in my 85GT.  I arrived home at 5:45 PM and all is well. Oh yeah, this car now has 212,000 miles. I certainly can't complain about anything. Now for the next couple of weeks my son and I will be fixing a couple minor things....the cruise control, the AC and the front rotors. We will also be doing some neccessary routine things to get it ready for the Utah winter. Well, I am about dead from the Dana Point turnaround and it's getting late. Good night y'all.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>P.S. DAD, The car is for my son, right now. Later, it wil be mine, oh yes, it will be mine....BWAHAAAAHAHAHAHA!!!! It told him that when he gets ready to sell it, he knows where to look  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>PEACE!!!<BR>  <p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 07-15-2001).]||||reg||12
